{"strongs": "H7493", "word": "רָעַשׁ", "translit": "ra.ash", "root": "רעש", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "quake, shake", "definition": "[ רָעַשׁ ] verb quake, shake , intransitive (Late Hebrew = Biblical Hebrew, so Aramaic (rare), and (once) רְשְַׁ toss, rage (of sea); Arabic , usually , , (loan-word?), tremble, quiver, quake ; compare perhaps Assyrian rêšu , exult ); — Qal Perfect 3 feminine singular רָעֲשָׁה Jer 8:16 ; Jer 49:21 , רָעָ֑שָׁה Judg 5:4 ; Ps 68:9 3 plural רָעֲשׁוּ Joel 2:10 +, etc. Imperfect 3 masculine singular יִרְעַשׁ Ps 72:16 , 3 feminine plural תִּרְעַשְׁנָה Ezek 26:10 , etc.; Participle plural רֹעֲשִׁים Jer 4:24 — quake, shake , of earth Judg 5:4 = Ps 68:9 , 2Sam 22:8 (|| רגז ) = Ps 18:8 (|| id. ), Ps 77:19 (+ רגז ), also Isa 13:13 (with עַלכֵּֿן , + מִמְּקוֺמוֺ , pregnantly; || רָגַז ), Jer 51:29 with מִן causative Jer 8:16 ; Jer 10:10 ; Jer 49:21 of מוֺסְדֵי אָ֑רֶץ Isa 24:18 of heavens Joel 2:10 ( לִפְנֵי causative; || רָגַז ); heavens and earth Joel 4:16 mountains Jer 4:24 ; Nah 1:5 ( מִן person causative ), Ps 46:4 ( ב causative ); walls Ezek 26:10 ( מִן causative ); אִיִּים v Ezek 26:15 (id.); מִגְרשׁוֺת Ezek 27:28 ( ל causative ); הַסִּפִּים Amos 9:1 all living things Ezek 38:20 ( מִפָּנַי causative ); of waving grain Ps 72:16 . Niph`al נִרְעֲשָׁה הָאָרֶץ Jer 50:46 is made to quake ( מִקּוֺל ). Hiph`il Perfect 2 masculine singular הִרְעַשְׁתָּה Ps 60:4 1 singular הַרְעַשְׁתִּי Ezek 31:16 ׳ וְהִר consecutive Hag 2:7 Imperfect 2 masculine singular suffix 3 masculine singular (הֲ)תַרְעִישֶׁנּוּ Job 39:20 Participle מַרְעִישׁ Isa 14:16 + 2 t.; — 1. cause to quake , subject ׳ י , with accusative of heavens, earth, nations, etc., Hag 2:6 ; Hag 2:7 ; Hag 2:21 , compare Ps 60:4 nations + מִקּוֺל Ezek 31:16 subject man, with accusative of kingdoms Isa 14:16 (|| מַרְגִּיז ). 2. cause (horse) to spring, leap (like locust), man subject, Job 39:20 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8039')\">BDB8039</entry> [<entry onclick